   $q$The prefix re- can mean "back," and the Latin root ject means "throw." What does it mean that the judges "did not reject the result"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They refused to look at the video of the finish","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"They threw the baton back to Dalia after the race","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"They decided the race needed to be run again","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-prefix-as-again"},{"text":"They accepted the result instead of throwing it out","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They accepted the result instead of throwing it out$q$, $q$To reject is to "throw back" or refuse, so not rejecting the result means the judges let it stand. Reading re- as "again" suggests a rerun, but nothing in the text says the race was run again.$q$, 'draft', '1062a784-bfcb-5328-ba64-5da8d5c830ef')
