   $q$The prefix trans- means "across," and the Latin root port means "carry." What do animals do when they "transport seeds"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They eat seeds and destroy them for good","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"They carry seeds from one place to another","is_correct":true},{"text":"They keep seeds safe in a single spot","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"They plant seeds deep in the ground","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They carry seeds from one place to another$q$, $q$Transport means "carry across," which matches a deer carrying a burr a long distance and birds dropping seeds miles away. Keeping seeds in one spot is the opposite of carrying them across a distance.$q$, 'draft', 'ddd97707-5194-5811-90cf-ed551eae73fa')
