   $q$The prefix uni- means "one." Why did performers need to balance when they rode a "unicycle"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It has no pedals, so riders push with their feet","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"It has three wheels that turn in different ways","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-prefix-meaning"},{"text":"It has a giant front wheel and a tiny rear wheel","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-similar-word"},{"text":"It has only one wheel to rest on","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It has only one wheel to rest on$q$, $q$Uni means "one," and the passage says performers balanced on a single wheel. The giant front wheel describes a different, older bicycle that still had two wheels.$q$, 'draft', '98c91e10-4d4f-529e-8c24-b36cde61f489')
