insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('b61e01fc-665f-5c02-abc0-f08a9871079d', 'rg6-word-parts-p07', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g6-word-parts'), null,
        '6-8', $q$Opening Night$q$, $q$For six weeks, the drama club had rehearsed a play about a lost explorer and a talking parrot. Amina Diallo played the explorer, and she knew every line by heart. Still, on opening night, her hands would not stop shaking.

Before the curtain rose, Mr. Kowalski, the director, gathered the cast in a circle. He reminded them to project their voices so the people in the last row could hear. "Speak to the back wall," he said, "not to the floor."

The first scene went smoothly. Then, in the middle of the second scene, the music stopped abruptly. The sound board had lost power. For a moment, the stage was silent, and Amina felt every eye in the theater on her.

She remembered something Mr. Kowalski had said in rehearsal. If something goes wrong, stay in character. So Amina turned to the boy playing the parrot and improvised a line. "Even the jungle has gone quiet," she said. "Something must be watching us." The audience laughed, and the parrot squawked right on time.

A minute later, the power returned, and the music began again. After the show, the stage crew apologized for the interruption. Amina told them it had been her favorite moment. The audience never knew the silence was a mistake, and some people thought it was the best part of the play.$q$, 'draft')
