   $q$The prefix pro- means "forward," and the Latin root ject means "throw." What did Mr. Kowalski want the cast to do when he told them to "project their voices"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Show their lines on a large screen above the stage","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-word-meaning"},{"text":"Send their voices forward so people far away could hear","is_correct":true},{"text":"Practice their lines one more time before the show","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"Keep their voices low so the music could be heard","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Send their voices forward so people far away could hear$q$, $q$Project means "throw forward," and he wanted people in the last row to hear, telling the cast to speak to the back wall. Showing words on a screen is a different meaning of project that does not fit this sentence.$q$, 'draft', 'b61e01fc-665f-5c02-abc0-f08a9871079d')
