   $q$The prefix im- can mean "not," pro- can mean "ahead," and the root vis means "see." What did Amina do when she "improvised a line"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She improved a line so it sounded better than before","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-similar-word"},{"text":"She said a line she had practiced for six weeks","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"She looked ahead in the script to find her next line","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-literal-root"},{"text":"She made up a line on the spot without planning it","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She made up a line on the spot without planning it$q$, $q$Improvise means to do something "not seen ahead," so Amina invented a new line when the music stopped. "Improved" looks similar, but she was not fixing an old line; she was creating one that was never in the script.$q$, 'draft', 'b61e01fc-665f-5c02-abc0-f08a9871079d')
