   $q$The words "abruptly" and "interruption" share the root rupt, meaning "break," and inter- means "between." What was the "interruption" the stage crew apologized for?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The time between the first scene and the second scene","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"},{"text":"The funny line Amina spoke to the boy playing the parrot","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"The break in the middle of the show when the music stopped","is_correct":true},{"text":"The laughter from the audience at the end of the play","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The break in the middle of the show when the music stopped$q$, $q$An interruption is a break that comes between, and the crew apologized because the power loss stopped the music in the middle of a scene. Amina's line was her response to the interruption, not the interruption itself.$q$, 'draft', 'b61e01fc-665f-5c02-abc0-f08a9871079d')
