   $q$The Greek root geo means "earth," and the ending -ologist means "one who studies." What do the "geologists" on the team study?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The rocks and soil that make up the earth","is_correct":true},{"text":"The stars and planets far beyond the earth","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-root-meaning"},{"text":"The maps that show where objects were found","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-similar-word"},{"text":"The bones of animals that people once ate","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The rocks and soil that make up the earth$q$, $q$Geo means "earth," so geologists study the earth, and the passage says they study the layers of rock and soil. Animal bones are clues about food, which archaeologists study, not geologists.$q$, 'draft', '3e17d36b-ab5d-51df-aaeb-b87570eeb1d4')
