   $q$The prefix re- means "again," con- means "together," and the Latin root struct means "build." What does the team do when it "reconstructs broken objects"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It breaks the objects into smaller pieces to study them","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"It builds the objects again by fitting the pieces together","is_correct":true},{"text":"It makes brand new copies of the objects for the museum","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It cleans the dirt off the objects with soft brushes","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It builds the objects again by fitting the pieces together$q$, $q$Reconstruct means "build together again," and the next sentence describes fitting the pieces of a pot back together. Cleaning happens too, but the word itself is about rebuilding, not washing.$q$, 'draft', '3e17d36b-ab5d-51df-aaeb-b87570eeb1d4')
